OL,3,GNEWSAPolitical rivals join forces to
OL,4,Aclear footpath
OL,5,
OL,6,FCity councillors from opposing parties
OL,7,Fhave come together to clear weeds and
OL,8,Frubbish from a footpath in
OL,9,FPeterborough.
OL,11,FFletton and Woodston's Reform
OL,12,Fcouncillor, Andrew O'Neil, joined
OL,13,FGreens Ed Murphy and Katherine Sharp to
OL,14,Fwork on a section of Woodston footpath,
OL,15,Fconnecting Wareley Road to Pleasure
OL,16,FFair Meadow Road.
OL,18,FThe three said they were happy to work
OL,19,Fwith others from across the political
OL,20,Fspectrum to put residents first and
OL,21,Fresolve local problems.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
FL,379,370,200,160,0,100
